[{"q":"Security education teaches us to stay ____.","options":["afraid of everyone forever","silent in class always","safe","away from school"],"answer":2,"explain":"Be alert, not fearful."},{"q":"If a stranger asks you to go with them, you should ____.","options":["say no and tell an adult","enter the car","follow quietly","keep it secret"],"answer":0,"explain":"Never go with a stranger."},{"q":"Do not put ____ in sockets.","options":["fingers or metal","the plug of a safe appliance","nothing always including plugs","a charger the right way"],"answer":0,"explain":"Electric shock is dangerous."},{"q":"In a fire, ____ to the nearest exit.","options":["go back for toys first always","hide under a nylon bag","move quickly and calmly","use the lift in a burning house if told never"],"answer":2,"explain":"Know the escape route. Don’t use lifts in a fire."},{"q":"When the alarm rings, ____.","options":["follow emergency instructions","run in any direction screaming only","lock yourself in the toilet always","ignore it"],"answer":0,"explain":"Practise drills seriously."},{"q":"Report suspicious bags in public to ____.","options":["security / police","your younger sibling only","a stranger to open it","nobody"],"answer":0,"explain":"Do not touch unknown packages."},{"q":"Online, do not share your ____.","options":["class","first name only with teacher","address and password","favourite subject"],"answer":2,"explain":"Personal data can be misused."},{"q":"Do not take ____ given by friends without an adult’s knowledge.","options":["a textbook","unknown drugs or tablets","your own lunch","your own water bottle"],"answer":1,"explain":"Unknown substances can harm you."},{"q":"Flood safety: do not walk in ____ water.","options":["a shallow known gutter at home never anyway wait","a bath","a puddle with an adult on the compound","fast or deep"],"answer":3,"explain":"Flood water can hide holes and germs."},{"q":"Do not take gifts from ____.","options":["strangers","your parents","your teacher as a prize","grandparents"],"answer":0,"explain":"Strangers may not be safe."},{"q":"Cyber predators may pretend to be ____.","options":["your parent at home","children or friends","your head teacher in person","the school bell"],"answer":1,"explain":"Never meet an online stranger alone."},{"q":"A good security habit at home is to ____ the door.","options":["lock","leave wide open at night always","hide the key under the mat always","tell strangers where the key is"],"answer":0,"explain":"Lock doors and windows."},{"q":"If you get lost in a market, ____.","options":["follow any stranger home","hide in a boot of a car","stay put and look for a security post / tell a seller with a stall to find police","leave town"],"answer":2,"explain":"Stay visible and ask official help."},{"q":"Wear a ____ in a car.","options":["seat belt","loose scarf on the door","blindfold","school bag on the head"],"answer":0,"explain":"Seat belts save lives."},{"q":"The assembly point is where we ____ in an emergency.","options":["buy snacks","play football first","meet","hide from teachers"],"answer":2,"explain":"Schools have assembly points."},{"q":"School ID and visitors’ passes help to ____.","options":["know who belongs","play football","cook","decorate only"],"answer":0,"explain":"Visitors should report at the gate."},{"q":"A whistle can be used to ____ for help.","options":["sweep","call","cook","iron"],"answer":1,"explain":"Loud signals attract attention."},{"q":"Do not walk alone in ____ places.","options":["dark lonely","your living room","a supervised playground","a busy school corridor"],"answer":0,"explain":"Stay where people can see you."},{"q":"Bullying should be ____.","options":["praised","reported","kept as a secret always","copied"],"answer":1,"explain":"Tell a teacher."},{"q":"When cycling, wear a ____.","options":["blindfold","long loose scarf in the wheel","earphones at full volume always","helmet"],"answer":3,"explain":"Helmets protect the head."},{"q":"Medicines at home should be kept ____.","options":["next to sweets","on the floor","out of children’s reach","in drink bottles"],"answer":2,"explain":"Wrong medicine is dangerous."},{"q":"Do not fight. Fighting can cause ____.","options":["injury","better exam scores","peace always","more friends always"],"answer":0,"explain":"Use words or a teacher, not fists."},{"q":"Nigeria’s national emergency number is ____.","options":["911 only as the only option","000","1234","112"],"answer":3,"explain":"112 is the national emergency number."},{"q":"When crossing the road, look ____, right and left again.","options":["backwards only","at your phone only","left","at the sky only"],"answer":2,"explain":"Stop, look and listen."},{"q":"Your body is private. If someone touches you in a bad way, ____.","options":["tell a trusted adult","hide at the market","keep silent forever","blame yourself"],"answer":0,"explain":"It is not your fault. Speak up."},{"q":"A strong password should not be ____.","options":["1234 or your name","secret","a mix of letters and numbers","long"],"answer":0,"explain":"Guessable passwords are weak."},{"q":"If you are in danger, tell a ____ adult.","options":["trusted","nobody","unknown online only","a stray animal"],"answer":0,"explain":"Parents, teachers and police can help."},{"q":"In a stampede, move ____ the crowd if you can, protect your chest.","options":["against blindly","deeper into","by sitting in the middle","sideways out of"],"answer":3,"explain":"Protect yourself; don’t push."},{"q":"Do not play with ____.","options":["puzzles","a football in a field","story books","fire and matches"],"answer":3,"explain":"Fire can burn."},{"q":"The police emergency number often taught is ____.","options":["0000","12","199","7777"],"answer":2,"explain":"199 can reach the police."},{"q":"Which is a safe action?","options":["running across a highway","keeping abuse secret","telling a teacher about bullying","swimming in a flood"],"answer":2,"explain":"That action hel